{"id":"645e05e0-6db5-40f1-9b60-e99f99a7ec61","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"13741dbe1a230a2d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"59433c8620975d177209fa66f79c1712187a6fcc","start":2194,"end":2218},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","list","\"",":","(",")","=>","RunInfo","[]",";"]},"context":{"before":"4264f6d15a93130c","after":"571196d0837bd09b"}},"payload":{"text":"The running ones first (newest first), then the ones that ended (newest first).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:08.655Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:08.655Z"}
{"id":"828e143e-1f3f-4af2-b54c-2d02a60f95e0","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1684ce65be9cb58b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d1d4d380d3f6c55b5d7c6af4d9a405fe29b1ff23","start":1773,"end":1826},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","end","\"",":","(","exitCode",":","number",",","stopped","?",":","boolean",")","=>","void",";"]},"context":{"before":"e24e8f6494a0dcdf","after":"82806e358b69d298"}},"payload":{"text":"It ended: by itself (`exited`, or `failed` with a nonzero code) or because it was stopped.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:11.445Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:11.445Z"}
{"id":"985e9861-6267-4043-be76-090752a1bea5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6a2d107664b30585","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8deac613d9db0f6db6c89d512740018f1de49f83","start":4474,"end":4550},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["hub",".","publish","(","\"","session.event","\"",",","{","\"","name","\"",":","\"","run.started","\"",",","\"","detail","\"",":","info",".","kind","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"87395f1e18a4b073","after":"296b29d3024c1b2a"}},"payload":{"text":"The session timeline (packages/api/README.md O6): a run's kind, not what it ran.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:37.735Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:37.735Z"}
{"id":"a99ef076-bb5d-4242-8868-bfc7e84cd3d4","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"4f9b14a1b821e839","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"e7cd6061d9299d6326326fa6585675430bdd434c","start":2538,"end":2616},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","runningService","\"",":","(","matches",":","(","run",":","RunInfo",")","=>","boolean",")","=>","RunInfo","|","undefined",";"]},"context":{"before":"3fe27bace657677c","after":"9003b4318043ea37"}},"payload":{"text":"The running service that `matches`, if any — a second `vite` in the same directory finds the first.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:05.430Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:05.430Z"}
{"id":"b282cf02-a1b2-43fe-b5f7-eccca8268e3c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"83fe7547ba67fcbb","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c36b81adfd420c55a6c86e1c340666424c8fc654","start":1500,"end":1590},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","update","\"",":","(","change",":","Partial","<","Pick","<","RunInfo",",","\"","port","\"","|","\"","title","\"","|","\"","kind","\"","|","\"","runtime","\"",">",">",")","=>","void",";"]},"context":{"before":"5cdcd9200d49b364","after":"e24e8f6494a0dcdf"}},"payload":{"text":"A task that turns out to keep running (it started listening) becomes a service.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:16.029Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:16.029Z"}
{"id":"cce2f114-2d35-413d-b1bf-50debcc9b08f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3fe27bace657677c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b65f8ae30cdf1dbfd311dbc141fc24de84e925a6","start":2404,"end":2436},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","restart","\"",":","(","id",":","string",")","=>","void",";"]},"context":{"before":"571196d0837bd09b","after":"4f9b14a1b821e839"}},"payload":{"text":"Start a running run over, if it can be: the same run, by a dev server's own account of how.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:07.200Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:07.200Z"}
{"id":"d7b3e6b4-e3c4-4ed2-ae12-5a4fdff40dcd","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"787aac459834092f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d21bcb5353c976b52c56f4a9960c4d08068ff5e8","start":3123,"end":3147},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","KEEP_SAID","=","64_000"]},"context":{"before":"70776b0abd510759","after":"32d7430f7fda350b"}},"payload":{"text":"How much of what a running run's said is kept, its latest: what someone following it from later still reads.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:42.106Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:42.106Z"}
{"id":"e8288f5e-dc0f-4844-a1d0-0bd0e6c6e1b6","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"49bb84d65b0b5eec0bdc4fe2937daa7b1f22e312","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"dcaab3599d411597"}},"payload":{"text":"What's running, in one place: every run the editor starts — a terminal's `node` script or `vite` dev server (and so\n`npm run …`, which runs them) — is registered here as it starts and marked as it ends, so the editor can show what's\nrunning, stop any of it, and refuse to start a second copy of a service that's already up.\n\nA run is a **service** (a dev server: runs until stopped) or a **task** (a script: runs to completion). The registry\nkeeps the running ones and the last few that ended, and serves them (`runs.list`) and stopping one (`runs.stop`).\n\nIt's the core runtime's own account, read by the shell's run picker, profile-files.ts (where a profiled preview's dev\nserver serves) and agents (debug-mcp's `runs`). A run's id is the one everything about the run carries — the runner's\n`node.start`, a debug session's launch config, a preview's production session — so what's learned from a run (its\ncoverage, its profiles, the capabilities it used) can be put together as one record. Ids are UUIDs: records outlive\nthe page. VS Code's \"what's running\" is the `running` extension's, from VS\nCode's own API (terminal shell integration, debug sessions, tasks), as it would be on the desktop.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:17.395Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:17.395Z"}
{"id":"f08fa403-8298-4937-a920-199d646a0eac","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"d50989721a0e7c66","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/runs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"55d9f801a8bd23e7c857d5966a685e4b9e7428f5","start":3829,"end":4003},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","list","=","(",")",":","RunInfo","[]","=>","[","...","[","...","running",".","values","(",")","]",".","map","(","(","run",")","=>","run",".","info",")",".","sort","(","(","left",",","right",")","=>","right",".","startedAt","-","left",".","startedAt",")",",","...","ended","]",".","map","(","(","info",")","=>","(","{","...","info","}",")",")"]},"context":{"before":"9c21e33fad45525c","after":"03b96d9948f25a79"}},"payload":{"text":"Copies: a caller in this realm gets the list itself, not a clone, and must not see a run change under it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:39.208Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:01:39.208Z"}
